# 44. EXAM TRAPS

### Trap 1

> **"Red Team means unauthorized hacking."**

False.

A legitimate Red Team operates with authorization and defined scope.

---

### Trap 2

> **"Blue Team only uses antivirus."**

False.

Blue Teams use many capabilities including SIEM, EDR, network monitoring, threat intelligence, threat hunting, and incident response.

---

### Trap 3

> **"Purple Team means a third team that attacks both sides."**

False.

Purple Team generally describes collaboration between offensive and defensive functions.

---

### Trap 4

> **"Penetration testing and Red Teaming are exactly the same."**

False.

They overlap but usually have different scope and objectives.

---

### Trap 5

> **"Red Team success means compromising the most systems."**

False.

The goal is to test defined security objectives and identify weaknesses within authorization.

